WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
Census forms ask which
ethnic group you belong to,

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.870
and offer a set of boxes to tick.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.930
The ONS describes ethnic group as
subjectively meaningful to an individual.

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.030
It adds that the choice is constrained
and influenced by the options presented.

5
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.750
So does it come down to how people look?

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.270
Where they were born?

7
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.230
Two neighbours share a
language and a passport.

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.980
Can they still belong to
different ethnic groups?

9
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:30.250
In this mission, you'll test the
markers often used to define ethnicity,

10
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.710
one by one.

11
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:38.110
Then you'll see how age, gender, place and
role shape the way identity is perceived.

12
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.590
Your mission: decide whether two neighbours
with one language and one passport

13
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.090
can belong to different ethnic groups.
